Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 16:20:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] docs: write up the five upstream compiler bugs

Five defects found while porting ACE to a host cross-compiler, all of
which affect the native AmigaOS build too, collected in a form that can be
handed to the maintainer: the use-after-free in change() that corrupts -O
output, the unchecked fopen() in fsize(), the NULL libname crash after a
failed DECLARE, the stray 0xFF byte on every generated .info, and the
first-dot extension handling.

Each entry names the file, quotes the offending code, states the effect
and how it was fixed here.  Also lists the smaller findings that were left
alone (bin/bas dropping options with -S, the stale ami.lib references) and
records what was and was not verified -- runtime behaviour on real
hardware was not, since this checkout has no bootable emulator.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
